#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Per-CPU detection of speculative execution vulnerabilities, kernel parameters Ditana applies by default, and how to verify or override them after installation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "CPU vulnerability mitigations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"Ditana enables CPU vulnerability mitigations in **High Security mode** by "
"default. The installer detects which mitigations your specific CPU needs by "
"reading `/sys/devices/system/cpu/vulnerabilities/`, then offers each as an "
"individually-toggleable checkbox in the **Expert Settings → CPU "
"Vulnerability Mitigation Options** dialog. This page documents every option "
"in detail."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Default kernel settings vs Ditana's mitigations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"The upstream Linux defaults balance security against performance and leave "
"certain vulnerabilities unmitigated unless explicitly opted in. Ditana opts "
"in by default — for most workloads the cost is negligible, while the "
"security benefit is substantial. You can revert any individual mitigation in "
"the installer if you have a workload that demonstrably benefits."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"The mitigation logic is hardware-specific. Only the vulnerabilities your CPU "
"actually exhibits are configured; everything else is left at the kernel "
"default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "After installation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"Several mitigations involve disabling Simultaneous Multi-Threading (SMT, "
"also known as Hyper-Threading) as a fallback. Ditana's [custom terminal "
"header](https://github.com/acrion/ditana-print-system-infos) shows which "
"mitigations are active and whether SMT is on or off."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "You can also verify with:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "lscpu\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"To compare performance with and without a specific mitigation, edit the "
"kernel command line for a single boot and remove the parameter associated "
"with the mitigation you want to test. On a ZFS installation, which is what "
"the Standard profile produces, that is accomplished via the ZFSBootMenu boot-"
"environment editor; on a system that boots through GRUB, press `e` at the "
"menu. The parameters are listed below under \"Applied parameter\" for each "
"entry. Reboot and run your real workload – synthetic benchmarks rarely "
"capture real impact."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"To make a change permanent on a ZFS installation, set the command line "
"within the boot environment:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"sudo zfs set org.zfsbootmenu:commandline=\"rw <options>\" ditana-root/ROOT\n"
"zfs get org.zfsbootmenu:commandline ditana-root/ROOT\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"To make it permanent on a system that launches via GRUB, edit `/etc/default/"
"grub`, find the `GRUB_CMDLINE_LINUX_DEFAULT` line (first save a backup), "
"remove the parameter, then run:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "sudo grub-mkconfig -o /boot/grub/grub.cfg\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"If a change prevents booting, edit the kernel command line in the GRUB menu "
"to recover, then repeat the edit and `grub-mkconfig`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mitigations Ditana enables by default"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spectre variant 2 — Branch Target Injection"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"Speculative execution exploit allowing attackers to read sensitive data via "
"mistrained indirect branch predictors. Ditana applies the full mitigation "
"(Indirect Branch Prediction Barrier always-on rather than conditional)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> All Spectre variant 2 mitigations can be forced on at boot time for all programs. This will add overhead as indirect branch speculations for all programs will be restricted.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: Spectre](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/spectre.html)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Spectre v2` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce Spectre Variant 2 Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `spectre_v2=on` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "L1 Terminal Fault (L1TF)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"Affects Intel CPUs, allowing unauthorized access to data in the L1 cache. "
"Ditana enforces full mitigation with aggressive cache flushing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> The kernel does not by default enforce the disabling of SMT, which leaves SMT systems vulnerable when running untrusted guests with EPT enabled.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: L1TF](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/l1tf.html)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `L1tf` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce L1 Terminal Fault Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `l1tf=full,force` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Microarchitectural Data Sampling (MDS)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"Allows attackers to sample data from CPU buffers. Full mitigation may "
"disable SMT if necessary."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> The kernel does not by default enforce the disabling of SMT, which leaves SMT systems vulnerable when running untrusted code.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: MDS](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/mds.html)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Mds` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce MDS Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `mds=full,nosmt` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "TSX Asynchronous Abort (TAA)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"Affects CPUs with Transactional Synchronization Extensions. Full mitigation "
"may disable SMT if required."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> TSX might be disabled if microcode provides a TSX control MSR. If so, system is not vulnerable.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: TAA](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/tsx_async_abort.html)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Tsx async abort` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce TSX Async Abort Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `tsx_async_abort=full,nosmt` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Meltdown (L1D flushing)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"Speculative execution exploit allowing kernel memory reads from userspace. "
"Ditana forces L1 data cache flushing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> The kernel command line allows to control the L1D flush mitigations at boot time with the option `l1d_flush=`. By default the mechanism is disabled.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: L1D flush](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/l1d_flush.html)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Meltdown` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce Meltdown Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `l1d_flush=on` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "MMIO Stale Data"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Data leakage from memory-mapped I/O. Full mitigation may disable SMT."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> `full,nosmt` — Same as `full`, with SMT disabled on vulnerable CPUs. This is the complete mitigation.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: MMIO stale data](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/processor_mmio_stale_data.html)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Mmio stale data` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce MMIO Stale Data Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `mmio_stale_data=full,nosmt` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Retbleed — Cross-Thread Return Address Predictions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"Speculative execution attack leaking return addresses. Auto-selected "
"mitigation may disable SMT."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> `auto,nosmt` — automatically select a mitigation, disabling SMT if necessary for the full mitigation.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: kernel parameters](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.html)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Retbleed` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce Retbleed Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `retbleed=auto,nosmt` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"See also [kernel.org: Cross-Thread Return Address Predictions](https://"
"www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/cross-thread-rsb.html)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Speculative Return Stack Overflow (SRSO)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"Speculative attacks via the return stack buffer. Combines IBPB barriers with "
"strict spectre_v2-user mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> `Mitigation: IBPB`: Similar protection as \"safe RET\" but employs an IBPB barrier on privilege domain crossings (User→Kernel, Guest→Host).\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: SRSO](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/srso.html)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Spec rstack overflow` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce SRSO Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `spec_rstack_overflow=ibpb spectre_v2_user=on` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Gather Data Sampling (GDS)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"Affects AVX instructions. Forces microcode mitigation, or disables AVX where "
"microcode is unavailable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> Specifying `gather_data_sampling=force` will use the microcode mitigation when available or disable AVX on affected systems where the microcode hasn't been updated to include the mitigation.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: Gather Data Sampling](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/gather_data_sampling.html)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Gather data sampling` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce Gather Data Sampling Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `gather_data_sampling=force` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Register File Data Sampling (RFDS)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "Allows sampling of data from CPU registers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> This parameter overrides the compile time default set by `CONFIG_MITIGATION_RFDS`.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: kernel parameters](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.html)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `lscpu` identifier | `Reg file data sampling` |\n"
"| Setting name | *Enforce RFDS Mitigation* |\n"
"| Applied parameter | `reg_file_data_sampling=on` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"See also [kernel.org: RFDS](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-"
"guide/hw-vuln/reg-file-data-sampling.html)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Vulnerabilities not exposed in the installer"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"The kernel performs maximum mitigation by default for these — there is "
"nothing for Ditana to add."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"Five more are reported by the kernel and named nowhere above, because Ditana "
"adds nothing to them either: Ghostwrite, Indirect Target Selection, old "
"microcode, TSA and VMSCAPE. The kernel decides what each of them needs from "
"the processor it finds and leaves the result where `lscpu` and `/sys/devices/"
"system/cpu/vulnerabilities/` show it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spectre variant 1 — Bounds Check Bypass"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> There is no guarantee that all possible attack vectors for Spectre variant 1 are covered.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: Spectre](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/spectre.html)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "`lscpu` identifier: `Spectre v1`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "iTLB multihit"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"`lscpu` identifier: `Itlb multihit`. See [kernel.org: iTLB multihit](https://"
"www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/multihit.html)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "SRBDS — Special Register Buffer Data Sampling"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"`lscpu` identifier: `Srbds`. See [kernel.org: SRBDS](https://www.kernel.org/"
"doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/special-register-buffer-data-"
"sampling.html)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Speculative Store Bypass (SSB)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> The kernel provides mitigation for such vulnerabilities in various forms.\n"
">\n"
"> — [kernel.org: spec_ctrl](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/userspace-api/spec_ctrl.html)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid "`lscpu` identifier: `Spec store bypass`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mitigation reduction — at your own risk"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"The installer also exposes two options that *reduce* mitigations. These "
"significantly increase your exposure to known CPU vulnerabilities. Use only "
"with a clear, justified reason."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Disable Intel Indirect Branch Tracking — `ibt=off`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"Turns off the kernel's Indirect Branch Tracking. IBT is the forward-edge "
"half of Control-flow Enforcement Technology – the hardware checks that every "
"indirect jump or call lands on an `endbr` instruction, which is what makes "
"jump-oriented and call-oriented programming hard. It is control-flow "
"integrity, not a speculative-execution mitigation: Branch Target Injection "
"is Spectre v2, elaborated upon earlier under `spectre_v2=on`. This kernel "
"parameter is **undocumented** in the official kernel parameters reference, "
"even though it is commonly enabled by default on certain distributions "
"without any explicit communication."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"The kernel documents the other half of CET, the user-space shadow stack, at "
"[shstk](https://docs.kernel.org/next/x86/shstk.html); IBT itself has no page "
"of its own there."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Disable all mitigations — `mitigations=off`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"This is **stronger than unchecking every individual mitigation** in the "
"dialog. With `mitigations=off`, the kernel skips *every* mitigation it knows "
"about — including the ones Ditana doesn't expose because they're on by "
"default. The performance ceiling rises; the security floor drops, hard."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"Only useful for benchmarks, air-gapped systems with full physical control, "
"or environments where you have categorically other defences."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"See [kernel.org: kernel parameters](https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/"
"admin-guide/kernel-parameters.html)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "Disclaimer"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"The guidance here is based on the [official CPU vulnerability documentation]"
"(https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/admin-guide/hw-vuln/index.html) and "
"the [kernel command-line parameter reference](https://www.kernel.org/doc/"
"html/latest/admin-guide/kernel-parameters.html). Different kernel branches "
"occasionally diverge from these defaults in subtle ways; our testing covers "
"the Ditana-supported kernels, but unusual hardware combinations can produce "
"edge cases."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/content/docs/under-the-hood/mitigations.md
msgid ""
"If you have a workload that benefits from a different default, or if you "
"find a CPU model where Ditana's detection is incomplete or incorrect: please "
"[open a GitHub issue](https://github.com/acrion/ditana-config/issues) or "
"email support@ditana.org. The detection logic is data, not code — so "
"improvements are usually a few KDL lines."
msgstr ""
